# There is almost nothing here on purpose.
#
# This file used to hold twelve settings. Every one of them is now a row in the
# `config` table, because the n8n instance runs with
# N8N_BLOCK_ENV_ACCESS_IN_NODE=true and `$env` resolves to undefined -- in Code
# nodes and in expressions alike, silently.
#
# The alternative was to turn that setting off, which would let any Code node
# in any workflow on the instance read DB_POSTGRESDB_PASSWORD, to save reading
# four numbers. Not a good trade on a box that also runs other automations.
#
# It turned out better anyway. A threshold in an environment variable has no
# history: you cannot ask when it changed or what the accuracy was under the
# old value. As a row it has an `updated_at`, and eval_runs.config records
# exactly which values produced each score. Changing one is:
#
#   UPDATE config SET value = '8000', updated_at = now()
#    WHERE key = 'min_followers';
#
# then re-run workflow 05 and compare. See n8n/sql/03-config.sql for every key
# and what it does.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# What is NOT in the config table, and must not be:
#
#   creator_prod postgres   a Postgres credential in n8n, id creatorPgCred001
#   the replay token        a Header Auth credential on the webhook in 04
#
# Both are credentials because n8n encrypts them with the instance key, so no
# Code node can read them. A token that authenticates a caller belongs there;
# a number that configures behaviour belongs in the table.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The only variables that matter are on the n8n service itself, and Coolify
# already sets them:
#
#   N8N_EDITOR_BASE_URL   n8n needs it for its own links. The workflows read
#                         their copy from config.editor_base_url, because they
#                         cannot read this one.
#
# Left deliberately empty. If you find yourself adding a value here, check
# first whether a Code node will actually be able to see it.
